Title: F1-M09 — The Foundry (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. RAIL WAGON COMMAND CAR - DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: rails ticking as the wagon cools, river water, a stove door clanging]]
[[MUSIC: restrained military tension]]

A plan of the foundry district lies on a folding table between two bunks. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it. RUSK sits on the lower bunk with a tally sheet.

RUSK
(gravelly)
The foundry is turning out vehicles faster than our crews can repair the damage they cause. A tank a minute from each hall. I have counted the wrecks; I know the rate.

MIRA
(serious)
A fuel depot sits outside the main wall. The production yard depends on it, but an armoured reserve is held underground.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: forward base west of the river, north and south fords, artillery ridge above the siding, fuel depot and tank wagons outside the wall, two assembly halls inside, slag heaps to the north]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(firm)
Cut the fuel supply first, then destroy the production yard. Do not give the reserve time to assemble.

RUSK
(economical)
Their pumps need seven minutes to fill the reserve. Seven minutes from the moment they see you near the depot, not from the moment you decide to hit it.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Siege guns reach ten cells. Their emplacements reach seven. Put the guns on the ridge and the depot cannot answer.

MIRA
(dry)
Or an engineer walks the siding with a charge. Quieter, and the pumps never start. Either way, the first sighting starts the clock.

RUSK
(irritated)
And when the depot goes, the tank wagons go with it. Stand well back.

MIRA
(analytical)
The fuel is not coming from the foundry, Captain. Somebody is shipping it in by rail. I want the siding office intact enough to read the tags.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
